living with a chronic disease like  cystic fibrosis is  a daily battle and even more difficult  during a pandemic  lauren milaski fierce is from las vegas  she has cf  she's not only defying the odds but  inspiring others along the way  we spoke with her about her journey  designer  fashion blogger author and mother lauren  malaski fierce  has accomplished a lot the past 37 years  and much more than doctors expected they  did not expect me to live much beyond  four or five lauren was diagnosed with  cystic fibrosis at just two days old  it's a chronic disease that affects your  lungs and digestive systems  she's developed more problems over the  years but her world completely changed  last summer  when one of her lungs collapsed talking  was  too much and laughing i couldn't laugh  imagine  breathing through a straw and that's it  24 7. her lungs were functioning at less  than  17 percent this was happening as coven  19  surged across the country because of  restrictions  her husband was allowed to stay with her  in the hospital  but she could only see her two children  once a week  for an hour at a time it was a very very  dark time  after a year on the wait list and living  in the hospital for four  long months lauren finally got the call  there was a match  she received a double lung transplant  this past october  very very grateful for all that i've  been given  and this you know second chance writing  has always been an outlet for lauren  she started a fashion blog years ago and  recently wrote a book called the sky  cracked open  it's a series of poems mostly written  for her kids  who she says are her motivation for  years my son  would use all of his wishes whether it  was like a birthday candle  or an eyelash or whatever for his mom to  get new lungs  those wishes came true lauren is still  quarantining at home with her family  but doing much better as dark as it is  there's always light and there's always  something to  be grateful for she is such an  inspiration this is a copy of her book  we were just talking about it's really  cute  made by the way it is cystic fibrosis  awareness month and lauren  has become an advocate for cystic  fibrosis and  john she has a second book now in the  works so  it's so good to see that she got that  and it was successful and she's doing  better  quite a prolific writer good stuff yeah  great story and fantastic does she  see that she is recovering all right
 

